    "result": "I implemented `check_password` in `solution.py` to follow the spec: it raises `TypeError` for non-`str` arguments and returns the violated codes in the required order (`LENGTH`, `CLASSES`, `USERNAME`, `REPEAT`, `BLOCKLIST`). The length check is inclusive of 12 and 64, the classes check counts ASCII lowercase, uppercase, digits, and \"other\" (including non-ASCII), and the username check only applies when the username has at least 3 characters. I wrote 39 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering each rule's boundaries, the case-sensitivity of the repeat rule, the blocklist's equality-only matching, and combined violations in order. `python -m pytest -q tests` reports all 39 passing. I did not run a coverage measurement, since the only permitted shell command is the test run, so the 90% line-coverage gate is unverified; by reading the code, every branch in `solution.py` should be exercised by the tests.",
